===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:talken<ety:inh<ang:*tealcian<ety:inh<gmw-pro:*talkōn>>>>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|talken}}, {{m|enm|talkien}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*tealcian|t=to talk, chat}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*talkōn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*talkōną|t=to talk, chatter}}, frequentative form of {{der|en|gem-pro|*talōną|t=to count, recount, tell}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dol-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*del-|t=to aim, calculate, adjust, count}}, equivalent to  {{m|en|tell}} + {{m|en|-k}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|nds|taalken|t=to chatter, gossip, talk}}. Related also to {{cog|bar|zoin|t=to pay}}, {{cog|cim|zaln|t=to pay}}, {{cog|nl|talen|t=to care, long; to speak; to say}}, {{cog|de|zahlen|t=to pay}}, {{cog|mhn|zoln|t=to pay}}, {{cog|da,nb|tale|t=to talk, speak}}, {{cog|fo,is,sv|tala|t=to speak, talk}}, {{cog|nn|tala|t=to speak, talk}}; also {{cog|la|dolus|t=deceit, deception, fraud, guile, treachery, trickery; malice; artifice, device, stratagem}}, {{cog|grc|δόλος|t=deceit, trick; wiles; bait}}, {{cog|hy|տող|t=line (in a text)}}. More at {{l|en|tale}}. Despite the surface similarity, unrelated to {{noncog|ine-pro|*telkʷ-|t=to talk}} (due to Grimm's law), which is the source of {{m|en|loquacious}}.
{{col-bottom}}

