===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|talk}}, {{m|enm|talke|t=conversation; discourse}}, from the verb (see above).

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[conversation]] or [[discussion]]; usually serious, but informal.
#: {{ux|en|We need to have a '''talk''' about your homework.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=XXIV|pages=198–199|pageref=198|passage=All this was extraordinarily distasteful to Churchill.{{...}}Never before had he felt such repulsion when the vicar displayed his characteristic bluntness or coarseness of speech. In the present connection&mdash;or rather as a transition from the subject that started their conversation&mdash;such '''talk''' had been distressingly out of place.}}
# A [[lecture]].
#: {{ux|en|There is a '''talk''' on {{w|Shakespeare}} tonight.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[gossip|Gossip]]; [[rumour]].
#: {{ux|en|There's been '''talk''' lately about the two of them.}}
# {{lb|en|preceded by {{m|en|the}}; often qualified by a following {{m|en|of}}}} A major topic of social [[discussion]].
#: {{ux|en|She is the '''talk''' of the day.}}
#: {{ux|en|The musical is the '''talk''' of the town.}}
# {{senseid|en|the talk}} {{lb|en|preceded by {{m|en|the}}}} A [[customary]] conversation by [[parent]](s) or [[guardian]](s) with their (often [[teenage]]) child about a [[reality]] of [[life]]; in particular:
## A customary conversation in which parent(s) explain [[sexual intercourse]] to their child.
##: {{ux|en|Have you had '''the talk''' with Jay yet? I found a condom in his room.}}
## {{lb|en|US}}<!--also elsewhere?--> A customary conversation in which the parent(s) of a [[black]] child explain the [[racism]] and [[violence]] they may face, especially when interacting with [[police]], and strategies to manage it.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Crystal McCrary|title=Inspiration: Profiles of Black Women Changing Our World|isbn=1613123442
|passage=Later, I made sure to have '''the talk''' with my son about being a black boy, {{...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Jim Wallis|title=America's Original Sin: Racism, White Privilege, and the Bridge|isbn=1493403486
|passage=All the black parents I have ever spoken to have had “'''the talk'''” with their sons and daughters. “'''The talk'''” is a conversation about how to behave and not to behave with police.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Stuart Scott; Larry Platt|title=Every Day I Fight|isbn=1101983175|page=36
|passage=Now, I was a black man in the South, and my folks had had “'''the talk'''” with me. No, not the one about the birds and bees. This one is about the black man and the police.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|not preceded by an [[article]]}} Empty [[boasting]], promises or claims.
#: {{ux|en|The party leader's speech was all '''talk'''.}}
# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural}} Meeting to [[discuss]] a [[particular]] [[matter]].
#: {{syn|en|conference|debate|discussion|meeting}}
#: {{ux|en|The leaders of the G8 nations are currently in '''talks''' over nuclear weapons.}}

